ência."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"At the town hall","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"At the town hall","lines":[["Chair","Welcome. Each speaker is limited to two minutes.","Bem-vindos. Cada orador tem dois minutos."],["Resident","May I submit a written comment instead?","Posso entregar um comentário escrito?"],["Chair","Certainly. Cards are at the door.","Claro. Os cartões estão na porta."],["Resident","Thank you. Will there be a vote?","Obrigado. Haverá votação?"]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Ritmo e ênfase para nuances","items":[{"label":"Ritmo e ênfase para nuances","note":"Ritmo e ênfase para nuances: o acento muda o sentido (He said she STOLE it × he said SHE stole it) e as pausas separam ideias técnicas densas.","words":["I didn’t SAY he did it.","I didn’t say HE did it.","I didn’t say he DID it."]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Announce a rule.","pt":"Anuncie.","model":"Speakers will be limited to two minutes."},{"q":"Give a notice with Please note.","pt":"Use.","model":"Please note that doors open at six thirty."},{"q":"Ask a procedural question.","pt":"Pergunte.","model":"May I raise a point of order?"}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a public notice (6 lines) for a neighbourhood meeting, with an agenda, a time limit and an accessibility note.","model":"NOTICE: Residents are cordially invited to a meeting on Friday, 12 July, at 6:00 p.m. in the Community Hall. Agenda: the new bus route; questions from the floor. Speakers will be limited to three minutes. Please note that the hall is step-free. Written comments will be accepted until Monday.","checklist":["Tom institucional","Usei **passiva** ou **will**"],"words":"6 linhas"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “open town hall” mean?","opts":["biblioteca 